From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:07:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: H616: dram: keep two 3/4-populated ranks contiguous

Some H616 TV boxes carry 1.5 GB of LPDDR3 as two ranks, each with 3/4 of
its rows populated; the Tanix TX1 V2.0's boot0 reports "32bit,2 ranks"
and para2 0x06001000. With the chip select above the row bits, each rank
spans a full 1 GiB and the missing quarter of rank 0, 0x70000000 to
0x7fffffff, is a hole inside RAM: writes there read back zero. The size
check probes 3/4 of 2 GiB, 0xa0000000, which rank 1 does back, and
reports 2 GiB; capped to 1.5 GiB, Linux still gets the hole and locks up.

Map the chip select below the two top row bits, so the missing rows sit
at 0xa0000000 and up, where mctl_calc_size() finds them and caps the
size at 1.5 GiB itself; the stock firmware also sees 1.5 GiB in one
piece, 0x40000000 to 0x9fffffff.
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
index 42a0550..e3dc607 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.c
@@ -141,6 +141,17 @@ static void mctl_sys_init(u32 clk_rate)
 	writel(0x8000, &mctl_ctl->clken);
 }
 
+/* Move row bit 'bit' (11 and up) one HIF bit higher. */
+static void mctl_row_bit_up(struct sunxi_mctl_ctl_reg *mctl_ctl, u8 bit)
+{
+	if (bit < 12)
+		mctl_ctl->addrmap[5] += 1 << 24;
+	else if (bit < 16)
+		mctl_ctl->addrmap[6] += 1 << (8 * (bit - 12));
+	else
+		mctl_ctl->addrmap[7] += 1 << (8 * (bit - 16));
+}
+
 static void mctl_set_addrmap(const struct dram_config *config)
 {
 	struct sunxi_mctl_ctl_reg * const mctl_ctl =
@@ -223,6 +234,19 @@ static void mctl_set_addrmap(const struct dram_config *config)
 		panic("Unsupported DRAM configuration: row number invalid\n");
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Two ranks of chips populated to 3/4 of their rows, as on 1.5 GB
+	 * LPDDR3 boards: with the chip select on top, the missing quarter of
+	 * rank 0 is a hole in the middle. Put the chip select under the two
+	 * top row bits, so the hole moves to the end and mctl_calc_size()
+	 * finds it. Not while probing rows, at 17.
+	 */
+	if (ranks == 2 && rows < 17) {
+		mctl_ctl->addrmap[0] = rows + cols - 5;
+		mctl_row_bit_up(mctl_ctl, rows - 2);
+		mctl_row_bit_up(mctl_ctl, rows - 1);
+	}
+
 	/* Bank groups, DDR4 only */
 	mctl_ctl->addrmap[8] = 0x3F3F;
 }
